#N canvas 20 20 27600 2940 12;
#X declare -path ../../Cut\ It;
#X obj 20 60 loadbang;
#X obj 20 120 del 31500;
#X msg 20 170 \; pd quit;
#X text 20 260 phone-assert-drive -- the driver half of the phone link's headless assertion run. It instantiates u_net pointed at 127.0.0.1 and pushes synthetic traffic onto disp \, exactly as m_nano \, m_organelle and u_err would. Nothing in the deployed patch is touched or rewritten., f 70;
#X text 20 400 RUN IT THROUGH test/gate/phone-assert.sh \, never by hand -- the analyser has to be bound to the port BEFORE u_net connects. Measured in Step 0: a UDP connect to a port with nothing listening survives exactly ONE datagram \, then ICMP kills the socket and every later send is discarded in silence. Start this by hand and you get one packet and then nothing \, which looks exactly like a broken rate limiter., f 70;
#X text 20 600 IT TESTS u_net IN ISOLATION \, not the whole instrument. The declare at the top of the file is what finds the abstraction from test/gate/. Driving the real u_tempo would make the status window depend on rounding that belongs to u_map \, and the contract under test here is only that u_net consumes disp and rate-limits what leaves., f 70;
#X obj 20 780 u_net 127.0.0.1 9995 9994;
#X obj 20 880 s \$0-tap-volca;
#X obj 300 880 s \$0-tap-p404;
#X text 560 600 THE ABSTRACTION UNDER TEST. Creation args are the phone's host and port and then THIS end's inbound port \, so pointing all three at the analyser costs nothing and exercises exactly the code path the phone gets. ITS TWO OUTLETS ARE THE VOLCA AND THE SP-404 \, and they leave here by NAME so no cord has to be drawn the length of the canvas., f 40;
#X obj 20 960 r \$0-mark;
#X obj 20 1010 t a a;
#X obj 240 1060 print MARK;
#X obj 20 1060 list append;
#X obj 20 1110 oscformat mark;
#X obj 20 1160 list prepend send;
#X obj 20 1210 list trim;
#X text 560 1180 list append BEFORE oscformat: a message box holding one word sends that word as a SELECTOR \, and oscformat wants a list. The same trap every branch out of g_oled's route has to dodge., f 70;
#X obj 560 1390 loadbang;
#X obj 560 1440 del 300;
#X msg 560 1490 connect 127.0.0.1 9995;
#X obj 20 1550 netsend -u -b;
#X obj 300 1390 r \$0-probebytes;
#X obj 300 1440 list prepend send;
#X obj 300 1490 list trim;
#X text 20 1610 THE DRIVER'S OWN NETSEND CONNECTS AT 300 ms \, u_net's at 1500 -- so the first mark is already in the stream before the thing being measured has said anything. Both point at the same port \, and the analyser tells them apart by OSC address., f 70;
#X obj 20 2400 loadbang;
#X obj 20 2450 del 2600;
#X msg 20 2500 connect 127.0.0.1 9994;
#X obj 20 2620 netsend -u -b;
#X obj 300 2450 r \$0-cmdbytes;
#X obj 300 2500 list prepend send;
#X obj 300 2550 list trim;
#X obj 20 1900 r presence;
#X obj 20 1950 list append;
#X obj 20 2000 oscformat probe presence;
#X obj 20 2050 s \$0-probebytes;
#X obj 400 1900 r \$0-tap-volca;
#X obj 400 1950 list append;
#X obj 400 2000 oscformat probe volca;
#X obj 400 2050 s \$0-probebytes;
#X obj 700 1900 r \$0-tap-p404;
#X obj 700 1950 list append;
#X obj 700 2000 oscformat probe p404;
#X obj 700 2050 s \$0-probebytes;
#X text 20 2180 u_net IS THE ONLY ABSTRACTION IN THIS RUN \, so nothing else can write presence and a re-wire seen here came from the inbound path or from nowhere. The two cords are the output devices -- wired rather than bussed \, per C-2 \, which is exactly why they need a tap at all., f 70;
